      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Debridement, either surgical or nonsurgical, can carry risks which nursing staff must be aware of in order to know how to react. Complications from bleeding, excessive debridement, exposure of vital tissue, pain, infections, delay in the healing process if the healing is insufficient, are some of the dangers which must be avoided."},
